    "description": "Pahlavani wrestling is an Iranian grappling tradition whose modern competitive form permits grips on specially designed trousers and a belt. It shares a historical background with zurkhaneh physical culture, while organized competition follows its own rules and tournament structures.",
    "tags": ["Pahlavani wrestling", "Grappling", "Traditional sports", "Wrestling rules", "Iranian sport"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "ready_for_review",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-28T07:10:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T07:10:18Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Pahlavani Wrestling: Technique, Tradition and Competition | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Understand Pahlavani wrestling, its distinctive clothing grips, relationship with zurkhaneh, and development as an international competition."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "distinctive-style",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Recognizing the wrestling style",
        "content": "Pahlavani wrestling is a contest between opponents seeking control through grappling and throws. A visible distinguishing feature is the clothing: wrestlers wear strong trousers extending below the knees, secured with a cloth belt. These garments are part of the technique because permitted grips include the trousers and belt. United World Wrestling’s account of the 2016 world championships describes leg trips, clinches, lifts, and throws within the style. [s1][s2]\n\nThe term *pahlavan* carries the meaning of hero or champion. That cultural vocabulary surrounds the sport, but a competitive result remains a specific sporting achievement. It should not automatically be treated as proof that an athlete fulfills every ethical ideal associated with the title. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "rules-and-reading",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "How the published rules frame a bout",
        "content": "The international rulebook hosted by United World Wrestling defines the objective as pinning an opponent or winning on points. Its clothing provisions specify a singlet, sturdy Pahlavani trousers, and a tightly secured cloth belt. Metal fittings are prohibited. The equipment rules make the clothing suitable for the grips that distinguish this form of wrestling. [s1]\n\nArticle 37 permits techniques used in freestyle and Greco-Roman wrestling, together with holds using the waist and knee areas of the trousers. The same rulebook provides a formal system for recording actions and resolving officials’ disagreements. Pahlavani competition therefore combines distinctive gripping possibilities with an organized framework of judging. [s1]\n\nThe inspected document is hosted in UWW’s March 2018 archive. It supports an explanation of that published framework, rather than a guarantee that every event through 2026 used identical provisions. Detailed scoring, eligibility, and bout procedures should be read against the regulations issued for a particular competition. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "gymnasium-relationship",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Related to the zurkhaneh, but historically changing",
        "content": "A zurkhaneh is a traditional house of strength associated with collective exercise and recitation. Wrestling formerly held a central place there. Chehabi’s historical account describes a subsequent separation: Pahlavani wrestling continued in a modernized competitive form while wrestling became less central within the gymnasium. This distinction prevents a sporting bout and an exercise session from being treated as interchangeable activities. [s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "international-competition",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A documented international milestone",
        "content": "UWW reported that the first World Pahlavani Wrestling Championships held under its supervision took place in Minsk in 2016. Iran finished ahead of Turkey and Russia in the team standings. This establishes a specific international competition milestone; it does not establish when the underlying tradition began or prove uninterrupted annual championships afterward. [s2]\n\nFor readers encountering the sport today, its most useful identifying features are its trouser and belt grips, its grappling contest, and its relationship with a broader Iranian vocabulary of strength and heroism. Keeping those features distinct makes both the sport and its cultural background easier to understand. [s1][s2][s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s3"]
      }
    ],
